      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Headache is a universal symptom. However, despite its prevalence and implications for daily living, headache epidemiology and its public health impact have only been partially documented. Most research has focused on migraine, with data on tension-type headache (TTH) being relatively sparse, especially for countries outside Western Europe and North America."},
